From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 17:27:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: ipad5: Wake from sleep on the Smart Cover

PMIC GPIO lines 0 and 10 are the Smart Cover hall sensors. Their events,
0x30 and 0x3a, latch while the iPad sleeps; list them as wake-only so
that opening the cover wakes the iPad. The polled switches are
unchanged: lines 0 and 10 are already outside gpio-reserved-ranges.

[Orchard: from orchard PR #118, commit e8b5e4b7; moved from the J71t
 board file to the shared iPad 5 file, so every iPad 5 model has it]

Assisted-by: LLM
---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s800x-ipad5.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s800x-ipad5.dtsi
index 2ce40b4..fc06d53 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s800x-ipad5.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s800x-ipad5.dtsi
@@ -182,6 +182,8 @@
 			interrupt-controller;
 			#interrupt-cells = <2>;
 			interrupts-extended = <&pinctrl_ap 76 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW>;
+			/* Smart Cover hall sensors (lines 0 and 10): wake only. */
+			apple,wake-events = <0x30 0x3a>;
 		};
 
 		tristar_charger: charger@180 {
-- 
